        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />

        <mxCell id="note1" value="compensate() is the saga-specific specialisation of undo(): both reverse execute(), but compensation must also work across service-owned data after a step has committed. run() executes the steps in order (reserve seat → create enrolment record → update schedule); if a step fails, compensate() is called on the completed steps in reverse order — all-or-nothing enrolment without a distributed transaction. Same Command pattern as page A applied to a second problem; Saga is only the architectural context." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;backgroundOutline=1;darkOpacity=0.05;fillColor=#FFF9B2;strokeColor=#B09500;size=14;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=6;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="40" width="380" height="150" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>

